  "title": "Attention Is All You Need - Wondering",
  "text": "Wondering\nHome\nExplore\nDocs\nSIGN IN\nAttention Is All You Need\n\nPaper by Ashish Vaswani et al.\n\nVaswani and colleagues introduce the Transformer, an encoder-decoder architecture built around attention rather than recurrence or convolution, and report its parallel training advantages, translation results, and transfer to constituency parsing.\n\n7 sections\n21 lessons\n~63 min\nVIEW PATH\nLEARNING MAP\nPERSONALIZE\n2 SOURCES\nWhat you will achieve\nUnderstand the Transformer architecture, its attention mechanisms, training design, and the results reported in the original paper.\nLearning Path\nAttention Is All You Need\n1. Motivation\n\n1/2 lessons\n\nRNN Limitations\n\nAttention-Only Model\n\n2. Core Architecture\n\n3/3 lessons\n\nEncoder-Decoder Stack\n\nEncoder Layers\n\nDecoder Masking\n\n3. Attention Mechanisms\n\n4/4 lessons\n\nAttention Basics\n\nDot-Product Attention\n\nMulti-Head Attention\n\nAttention Types\n\n4. Supporting Components\n\n3/3 lessons\n\nFeed-Forward Networks\n\nEmbeddings\n\nPositional Encoding\n\n5. Advantages of Self-Attention\n\n2/2 lessons\n\nComplexity Analysis\n\nLong-Range Dependencies\n\n6. Training Details\n\n4/4 lessons\n\nBatching Strategy\n\nTraining Efficiency\n\nLearning Rate Schedule\n\nRegularization\n\n7. Results and Impact\n\n3/3 lessons\n\nTranslation Results\n\nAblation Studies\n\nGeneralization\n\nLearning Map\nOPEN\nAttention Is All You Need\nMotivation\nCore Architecture\nAttention Mechanisms\nSupporting Components\nAdvantages of Self-Attention\nTraining Details\nResults and Impact\nRNN Limitations\nAttention-Only Model\nEncoder-Decoder Stack\nEncoder Layers\nDecoder Masking\nAttention Basics\nDot-Product Attention\nMulti-Head Attention\nAttention Types\nFeed-Forward Networks\nEmbeddings\nPositional Encoding\nComplexity Analysis\nLong-Range Dependencies\nBatching Strategy\nTraining Efficiency\nLearning Rate Schedule\nRegularization\nTranslation Results\nAblation Studies\nGeneralization\nJoined by 25 learners\nPREVIEW LESSON\nSTART LEARNING FOR FREE",
